{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>They have dealt corruptly with Him.</b> As the Targum renders: ״חַבִּילוּ לְהוֹן לָא לֵהּ״." "<b>His children's blemish.</b> They were His children, and the corruption that they corrupted is their blemish." "<b>His children's blemish.</b> It was the blemish of His children, and not His blemish." "<b>A crooked generation.</b> עָקֹם and מְעֻקָּל — as in ״וְאֵת כָּל הַיְשָׁרָה יְעַקֵּשׁוּ״ (Micah 3). And in Mishnaic language: ״חֻלְדָּה שֶׁשִּׁנֶּיהָ עֲקֻמּוֹת וַעֲקוּשׁוֹת״." "<b>And twisted.</b> אנטורט\"ילייש — like this פְּתִיל that one twists and wraps it around the גְּדִיל. פְּתַלְתֹּל is from doubled forms, like ״יְרַקְרַק״, ״אֲדַמְדָּם״ (Leviticus 13), ״סְחַרְחַר״ (Psalms 38), ״סְגַלְגַּל״ (Targum Yonatan, 1 Kings 7)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {4 "The la'az אנטורט\"ילייש appears to be Old French entortiller, 'to twist/tangle'."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:11.443154151Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}